\label{thm:thm1}
Let $\omega$ be a homogeneous Poisson Point Process (PPP) on $\Hd$ and let
$V_\omega:\Hd\to[0,\infty)$ be a continuous factor-of-$\omega$ potential with maximum norm 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:MainThmEq}
  \|V_\omega\|_\infty < \frac{(d-1)^2}{8}.  
\end{equation}
Then for a.e.\ $\omega$ and for all $x \in \Hd$, the tilted measures $\mathbf Q_T^x$ converge to a diffusion process that is independent of the starting point $x$.

