ref_dict.Cor Hecke twist standard and formal degr:
\begin{cor}
\label{Cor Hecke twist standard and formal degrees}
Let $\pi$ be an essentially square-integrable representation of $H$. Then $\gamma\cdot\pi$ is essentially square-integrable, and we have an equality of formal degrees
\[
d(K(s,N,\rho)=d(K(\gamma(s),N,\rho).
\]
More generally, if $\pi$ is a standard $H$-module, so is $\gamma\cdot\pi$, and twist by $\gamma$ also preserves genericity of the Langlands quotients.
\end{cor}

